cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this replication package, please cite the paper it accompanies
  (see preferred-citation below). Cite the software itself only if you use the
  estimation code independently of the paper.

title: "HMM-Decentralised-Perpetual-Futures: replication package for Same Formula, Different Signal"
abstract: >-
  Code, data and fitted parameters for a comparison of funding-rate censoring
  on the Hyperliquid, Binance and Bybit BTC perpetuals, a Gaussian hidden Markov
  model (K=3) on hourly Hyperliquid BTC perpetual log-returns and a
  Markov-switching AR(1) on the funding premium, including the multi-start
  protocol required to reach the maximum of the multi-modal MS-AR likelihood.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gelatotrade/HMM-Decentralised-Perpetual-Futures"
url: "https://github.com/gelatotrade/HMM-Decentralised-Perpetual-Futures"
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-08"
keywords:
  - regime switching
  - hidden Markov models
  - perpetual futures
  - funding rates
  - Hyperliquid
  - cryptocurrency market microstructure
  - Hamilton filter
  - censoring
  - Binance
  - Bybit
  - replication package

